# Update the installed LogicPad app

When you change the Tauri app (`04 Software/logicpad-app/`) or firmware the app talks to (HID protocol, vendor commands, store schema), also refresh the installed Windows program. Do not leave the user on an old Start-menu copy.

Daily use is `%LOCALAPPDATA%\LogicPad\LogicPad.exe` (Start menu / desktop shortcut), not `npm run tauri dev`.

## Build + install (agent runs this; never ask the owner to)

1. `taskkill /IM LogicPad.exe /F` if running.
2. From `04 Software/logicpad-app`, put Cargo on PATH (`%USERPROFILE%\.cargo\bin`).
3. **Force the project target dir** (must be absolute; a relative path resolves under `src-tauri/` and creates `src-tauri\src-tauri\target`):
   - `$env:CARGO_TARGET_DIR = "C:\...\logicpad\04 Software\logicpad-app\src-tauri\target"` before `npm run build:app`.
4. Run `npm run build:app` (or `Build LogicPad.bat` without `pause`).
5. Install **only** from:
   - `04 Software\logicpad-app\src-tauri\target\release\bundle\nsis\LogicPad_0.1.0_x64-setup.exe /S`
   - Never install from a temp/sandbox `cargo-target` path unless you have verified it is newer than the project target.
6. **Mandatory verify** (do not skip; do not tell the user the app is updated until this passes):
   - Compare `%LOCALAPPDATA%\LogicPad\LogicPad.exe` with `src-tauri\target\release\LogicPad.exe`.
   - **Length** must match exactly.
   - **LastWriteTime** on the installed exe must be within a few minutes of the built exe (same build).
   - If verify fails: close LogicPad, rerun install from step 5, verify again. If still wrong, rebuild with `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` set and repeat.
7. Start `%LOCALAPPDATA%\LogicPad\LogicPad.exe` (or tell the user to use Start menu after you start it).
8. If firmware/HID changed, remind that **Update firmware** with `LogicPad.bin` is still required on the pad.

## Common failure (do not repeat)

Saying “reinstalled” after `npm run build:app` when the sandbox wrote binaries elsewhere, or installing an older NSIS bundle while a newer compile exists. Always use project `src-tauri\target` and verify installed vs built exe size/time after `/S`.
